RULES TEXT (b), 35 words: You may make an offer only to a resident who will answer it before your own last turn, so that you still have a turn to deliver your side; the state lists who that is.
RULES TEXT (c), 58 words: Settlement. After round 8 every resident who still owes a side takes one settlement turn. Only its deliveries count; answers, offers and messages are ignored. Nobody sees anyone else's settlement choices before making their own, and all of them apply together, so you can deliver only goods you hold when settlement begins. Then projects complete and scores count.
